   "handbook.simpleradio_repeaters.troubleshooting.text_0": "Make sure your Relay shows READY and a positive ANT value, and that a Catalyst is installed.\n\nYou need at least one tuned Frequency Card in a Repeater Bank, or at least one RX card and one TX card in a Transponder.\n\nBeing able to talk from near Relay Tower 1 to a receiver near Relay Tower 2 does not guarantee that a signal from further away, such as Tower 5 or 6, can make the same jump.\n\nImprove the antenna, install an amplifier, or build more intermediary Relays to help weaker signals travel further.",
   "handbook.simpleradio_repeaters.terrain.title": "Terrain & Elevation",
-  "handbook.simpleradio_repeaters.terrain.text": "Overworld relay towers account for the landscape between them. A mountain across the path makes a signal travel farther, effectively. Masts at least eight blocks above the estimated ground avoid this extra loss. Higher antennas also receive a small, capped bonus to their antenna contribution.\n\nNear-ground signals receive at most a one-percent distance penalty above the surface. Below ground, the extra distance rises: 10% at eight blocks deep, 25% at sixteen, 50% at thirty-two, 100% at sixty-four, 150% at ninety-six and 200% at one hundred twenty-eight. Penalties are averaged along the path, not multiplied for every sample. A path entirely sixty-four blocks below ground has about half its normal range; one at one hundred twenty-eight has about one-third.\n\nClearance is measured between the tips of the two masts. Growing or trimming a mast updates its clearance during the normal ten-second antenna cycle. Adding spokes, changing cards, or aiming a receiver array reuses the terrain already measured. Saved towers retain their last verified mast height while unloaded.\n\nDuring terrain mapping, SCAN means there are no working links or previous terrain results yet. CHECK means mapping is pending while working links or previous results remain available. Existing paths keep their last verified penalty; a new path still waits for its first measurement, even if the Relay says CHECK. Breaking a wire or removing a tower still disconnects it immediately.\n\nTerrain is estimated from the world generator. Player buildings, tunnels and later excavation are not part of this approximation. The Nether, the End and dimensional focus projections keep their existing propagation rules.\n\nServer modes are Off, Relay Mapping (the default), and Full. Off restores original propagation and disables the elevation bonus. Full also checks ordinary radio and handheld connections; device links within 256 blocks remain unaffected.",
